    "question": {
      ":question/id": "98065fa7-27e8-527f-974b-cc88d87d902b",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/hard",
      ":question/problem": "Consider the augmented matrix $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}2 & 1 & 6 & 5 \\\\ 6 & 3 & 8 & 5 \\\\ -2 & -6 & 4 & -7\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nWhat matrix results from carrying out the following row operations on $T?$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R_{1} &\\leftrightarrow R_{3} \\\\ R_{3} &:=R_{3}+(-2)\\cdot R_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Let's list the required operations:\n\n- The operation $R_{1}\\leftrightarrow R_{3}$ means that we need to swap the first and third rows.\n\n- The operation $R_{3}:=R_{3}+(-2)\\cdot R_{2}$ means that we need to add $-2$ times the second row to the third row.\n\nApplying the operations, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T &= \\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}2 & 1 & 6 & 5 \\\\ 6 & 3 & 8 & 5 \\\\ -2 & -6 & 4 & -7\\end{array}\\right]\\,R_{1}\\leftrightarrow R_{3} \\\\ &\\sim \\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}-2 & -6 & 4 & -7 \\\\ 6 & 3 & 8 & 5 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 6 & 5\\end{array}\\right]\\,R_{3}:=R_{3}+(-2)\\cdot R_{2} \\\\ &\\sim {\\scriptsize \\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}-2 & -6 & 4 & -7 \\\\ 6 & 3 & 8 & 5 \\\\ 2+(-2)(6) & 1+(-2)(3) & 6+(-2)(8) & 5+(-2)(5)\\end{array}\\right]} \\\\ &\\sim \\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}-2 & -6 & 4 & -7 \\\\ 6 & 3 & 8 & 5 \\\\ -10 & -5 & -10 & -5\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$",
