    "question": {
      ":question/id": "443ef13a-7649-55ea-8d85-70a9862de513",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/hard",
      ":question/problem": "Consider the augmented matrix $U,$ given by\n\n$$\nU=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}0 & -7 & 7 & -7 \\\\ 2 & 2 & 0 & 6 \\\\ 3 & -2 & 6 & 9\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nWhat matrix results from carrying out the following row operations on $U?$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R_{2} &:=-3R_{2} \\\\ R_{1} &:=R_{1}+(-2)\\cdot R_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Let's list the required operations:\n\n- The operation $R_{2}:=-3R_{2}$ means that we need to multiply the second row of the matrix by $-3.$\n\n- The operation $R_{1}:=R_{1}+(-2)\\cdot R_{2}$ means that we need to add $-2$ times the second row to the first row.\n\nApplying the operations, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}U &= \\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}0 & -7 & 7 & -7 \\\\ 2 & 2 & 0 & 6 \\\\ 3 & -2 & 6 & 9\\end{array}\\right]\\,R_{2}:=-3R_{2} \\\\ &\\sim \\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}0 & -7 & 7 & -7 \\\\ -6 & -6 & 0 & -18 \\\\ 3 & -2 & 6 & 9\\end{array}\\right]\\,R_{1}:=R_{1}+(-2)\\cdot R_{2} \\\\ &\\sim {\\scriptsize \\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}0+(-2)(-6) & -7+(-2)(-6) & 7+(-2)(0) & -7+(-2)(-18) \\\\ -6 & -6 & 0 & -18 \\\\ 3 & -2 & 6 & 9\\end{array}\\right]} \\\\ &\\sim \\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}12 & 5 & 7 & 29 \\\\ -6 & -6 & 0 & -18 \\\\ 3 & -2 & 6 & 9\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$",
