      ":question/problem": "Consider the augmented matrix $M,$ given by\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}-9 & 8 & 8 & 6 \\\\ 1 & -4 & 3 & -3 \\\\ 3 & -4 & -1 & -4\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nWhat matrix results from carrying out the following row operations on $M?$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R_{1} &\\leftrightarrow R_{3} \\\\ R_{2} &:=R_{2}+(-1)\\cdot R_{1}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Let's list the required operations:\n\n- The operation $R_{1}\\leftrightarrow R_{3}$ means that we need to swap the first and third rows.\n\n- The operation $R_{2}:=R_{2}+(-1)\\cdot R_{1}$ means that we need to add $-1$ times the first row to the second row.\n\nApplying the operations, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M &= \\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}-9 & 8 & 8 & 6 \\\\ 1 & -4 & 3 & -3 \\\\ 3 & -4 & -1 & -4\\end{array}\\right]\\,R_{1}\\leftrightarrow R_{3} \\\\ &\\sim \\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}3 & -4 & -1 & -4 \\\\ 1 & -4 & 3 & -3 \\\\ -9 & 8 & 8 & 6\\end{array}\\right]\\,R_{2}:=R_{2}+(-1)\\cdot R_{1} \\\\ &\\sim {\\scriptsize \\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}3 & -4 & -1 & -4 \\\\ 1+(-1)(3) & -4+(-1)(-4) & 3+(-1)(-1) & -3+(-1)(-4) \\\\ -9 & 8 & 8 & 6\\end{array}\\right]} \\\\ &\\sim \\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}3 & -4 & -1 & -4 \\\\ -2 & 0 & 4 & 1 \\\\ -9 & 8 & 8 & 6\\end{array}\\right]\\end{aligned}\n$$",
